	(761, 'Better Homes and Gardens', '*Better Homes and Gardens* (stylized as Better Homes & Gardens and abbreviated as BHG) is the fourth most widely circulated magazine in the United States. *Better Homes and Gardens* focuses on interests regarding homes, cooking, gardening, crafts, healthy living, decorating, and entertaining. The magazine is published 12 times per year by Dotdash Meredith (formerly Meredith Corporation).\r\n\r\nBetter Homes and Gardens was founded in 1922 by Edwin Meredith, who  served as the United States Secretary of Agriculture under Woodrow Wilson and had previously founded the magazine *Successful Farming*. The original title was *Fruit, Garden and Home*. The name was changed to Better Homes and Gardens beginning with the August 1924 issue.\r\n\r\nISSN, WorldCat: 0006-0151\r\nOCLC: 5902855\r\n\r\nSubjects:; Architecture, Domestic; Architecture, Domestic Periodicals; Cooking; Cookbooks; Décoration intérieure Périodiques; Fruit-culture; Fruit-culture Periodicals; Gardening; Gardening Periodicals; Interior decoration; Interior decoration Periodicals; Jardinage Périodiques; Jardins Architecture Périodiques; Landscape gardening; Landscape gardening Periodicals; Periodical; Periodicals', NULL),
