	(1630, 'Luann Colombo', 'Luann Colombo, is a science, and health expert who has a bachelor\'s degrees in both Biology, and Psychology, as well as a master\'s degree in Science Education. She attended the \'State University of New York College at Oswego\' from 1974-1978. She has worked with such television programs as \'Bill Nye, the Science Guy\', the PBS science series \'NOVA\', as well as writing five books for \'Andrews and McMeel Publishing\'s \'Beakman\'s World\' products. She was the Outreach Manager, for the Pacific Science Center science museum in Seattle Washington. She is co-owner of Teknos Inc. a company that designs and builds interactive science exhibits. She has also worked with the \'National Safety Associates\', and the company \'Juice Plus\'. She has a husband, and lives with him, and his daughter in Littleton, Massachusetts.', NULL),
