	(4543, 'George Eliot', 'George Eliot, was an English novelist and one of the leading writers of the Victorian era. She is the author of seven novels, including The Mill on the Floss (1860), Silas Marner (1861), Middlemarch (1871–72), and Daniel Deronda (1876), most of them set in provincial England and well known for their realism and psychological insight. ([Source][1].)\r\n\r\n[1]: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Eliot', '1819-11-22'),
