	(4744, 'Howard Zinn', 'Howard Zinn (August 24, 1922 – January 27, 2010) was an American historian, playwright, and socialist thinker. He was chair of the history and social sciences department at Spelman College, and a political science professor at Boston University. Zinn wrote over 20 books, including his best-selling and influential A People\'s History of the United States. In 2007, he published a version of it for younger readers, *A Young People\'s History of the United States*.\r\n\r\nZinn described himself as "something of an anarchist, something of a socialist. Maybe a democratic socialist." He wrote extensively about the Civil Rights Movement, the anti-war movement and labor history of the United States. His memoir, *You Can\'t Be Neutral on a Moving Train* (Beacon Press, 2002), was also the title of a 2004 documentary about Zinn\'s life and work. Zinn died of a heart attack in 2010, at age 87. \r\n\r\n**Source**: [Howard Zinn](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Howard_Zinn) on Wikipedia.', '1922-08-24'),
