	(892, 'Quran', 'In 1968, Rashad Khalifa realized that the existing English translations did not present the truthful message of God’s Final Testament, the Quran. For example, two of the most popular translators (Yusuf Ali and Marmaduke Pickthall), could not overcome their corrupted religious traditions when it came to the Quran’s great criterion dealing with the worship of God alone (39:45). This distortion of the truth prompted him to translate the Quran himself.  This book comes to you with built-in physical evidence that it is God\'s message to you; it is mathematically composed far beyond human capability.', NULL),
	(893, 'Memories of the Body', NULL, NULL),
	(894, 'Maniac Magee', 'Jeffrey Lionel "Maniac" Magee might have lived a normal life if a freak accident hadn\'t made him an orphan. After living with his unhappy and uptight aunt and uncle for eight years, he decides to run--and not just run away, but run. This is where the myth of Maniac Magee begins, as he changes the lives of a racially divided small town with his amazing and legendary feats.', NULL),
