	(2601, 'No Gentle Love', 'The tale of Morgana, who is the object of desire for numerous men - the cousins who want to win her hand in marriage, for monetary gain only the madman that she has to murder in order to escape from him and the domineering Rian McShane.', NULL),
	(2602, 'My fourth-grade mess', NULL, NULL),
	(2603, 'Walking the trail', '"One fall morning Jerry Ellis donned a backpack and began a long, lonely walk: retracing the Cherokee Trail of Tears, the nine hundred miles his ancestors had walked in 1838. The trail was the agonizing path of exile the Cherokees had been forced to take when they were torn from their southeastern homeland and relocated to Indian Territory.\r\n\r\nFollowing in their footsteps, Ellis traveled through small southern towns, along winding roads, and amid quiet forests, encountering a memorable array of people who live along the trail today. Along the way he also came to glimpse the pain his ancestors endured and to learn about the true beauty of modern rural life and the worth of a man\'s character."--BOOK JACKET.', NULL),
